@startuml DomainModel
' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Domain model — single project-wide diagram, continuously evolved.
'
' Ownership over time (v0.9.3+):
'   - INITIAL DRAFT: Product Owner at M1, time-boxed ~1 hour. Drafts from
'     intakes / REQs only. Real-world entities only; no GUI; attributes only.
'   - REFINEMENT: Analyst at M2, time-boxed ~2 hours per UC. Adds entities
'     discovered via robustness analysis; types untyped attributes; prunes
'     state-machine entities; updates relationships.
'   - MAINTENANCE: Analyst on every change-impact event (REQ change flow,
'     Type 2 bug fix). M1 and M2 gates re-validate.
'
' Save as `domain-model/domain-model.puml` at the project root.
'
' Rules (full set in agents/iconix-product-owner.md rule 9 and
' agents/iconix-analyst.md `# Domain model rules`):
'
'   1. REAL-WORLD ENTITIES ONLY. No GUI classes. Pages, forms, screens
'      are NOT domain entities. (Examples to delete if you see them:
'      `WriteReviewPage`, `OrderForm`, `LoginScreen`.)
'
'   2. ATTRIBUTES ONLY, NO OPERATIONS. Operations come at M3 (Developer).
'      The Reviewer flags entity classes with operations and zero
'      attributes as "attribute-sparse" — fix at M2.
'
'   3. TYPE EVERY ATTRIBUTE. Untyped attributes (`+ name`, `+ data: any`)
'      are M2 blockers. Use real types: `string`, `int`, `decimal`,
'      `DateTime`, enum names, other entity names.
'
'   4. SKIP STATE-MACHINE ENTITIES. A "PendingQueue" is usually a STATE
'      on another entity, not a separate class. Ask: "is this a noun in
'      the business domain, or a phase of another noun?" If a phase,
'      model it as `entity.status: <enum>` instead of a separate class.
'
'   5. SHOW IS-A / HAS-A RELATIONSHIPS. Floating classes with no
'      relationships are an M1 smell — either link them, or question
'      whether they belong on the domain model at all.
'
'   6. DOMAIN MODEL = PROJECT GLOSSARY. Every noun in UC text must
'      appear here (or on a referenced sub-diagram). The PO's M1
'      checklist enforces this.
'
'   7. TIME-BOX: ~1 hour for typical scope. This is a glossary-as-
'      diagram, not a finished class model. The Analyst refines it.
'
'   8. MARK PO AMBIGUITIES with `' VERIFY:` comments placed IMMEDIATELY
'      ABOVE the ambiguous class declaration (not inside the `{ }`
'      block — PlantUML treats `'` mid-block lines inconsistently).
'      When you (the PO) are unsure whether something is a real entity
'      or a state/value/noun-from-the-business, write a `' VERIFY:`
'      comment block explaining your reasoning and what the Analyst
'      should validate at M2. Mirrors the `[VERIFY]` convention from
'      intake templates. See the PendingReviewsQueue example below.
' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' >>> REPLACE THE EXAMPLE BELOW WITH YOUR PROJECT'S DOMAIN ENTITIES. <<<
' >>> The Customer / Book / CustomerReview classes below are a worked  <<<
' >>> example (Internet Bookstore). Delete them and write your own.    <<<
' ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

class Customer {
  + id : int
  + email : string
}

class Book {
  + id : int
  + title : string
}

class CustomerReview {
  + id : int
  + bookId : int
  + customerId : int
  + reviewText : string
  + rating : int
  + status : ReviewStatus
}

enum ReviewStatus {
  Pending
  Approved
  Rejected
}

' Example of `' VERIFY:` convention (rule 8) — delete this block when
' you replace the example. Keep the convention itself in your real
' domain model whenever you (the PO) are unsure about an entity.
'
' VERIFY: Is PendingReviewsQueue a real entity (separate infrastructure
' container per iconix.config.yaml) or just the "pending" state of
' CustomerReview.status? The heuristic returns both. Analyst:
' resolve at M2 — keep as entity OR collapse into status enum on
' CustomerReview.
class PendingReviewsQueue {
}

' Relationships
Customer "1" -- "0..*" CustomerReview : writes
Book     "1" -- "0..*" CustomerReview : has
CustomerReview "0..*" -- "1" PendingReviewsQueue : queued in

@enduml
